# Records of phases 1 and 2 brought up to date after phase 3 — part 5. Assessed against the code on 2026-09-27.
#
# Each record in UPDATES replaces the record of the same number in docs/requirement-status.json (or, for a
# requirement that was PLANNED, its reason in docs/requirement-planned-notes.json). What the earlier record said and
# is still true is carried over; what Phase 3 added is named as such. No status was lowered.
# A record that was PLANNED with no note (Phase 1, never assessed one by one) says what Phase 3 added, and names what
# earlier phases hold only where that was read in the code or is recorded under another requirement.
#
# Facts that apply to many records below (verified in the code):
#   * A workflow of the Scenario Studio (src/pages/Studio.tsx, src/pages/FlowDesigner.tsx, src/pages/FlowCase360.tsx,
#     supabase/migrations/0017_scenarios_flows.sql) is a straight line of steps of nine kinds — request, approval,
#     release of money, evidence, settlement, accounting, reconciliation, review, notice. It is started by a person
#     (triggers manual and form; ten others are recorded as intent). It posts nothing and releases nothing: a release,
#     settlement or accounting step is complete only when it points to the record that did it. Its money flow,
#     accounting, settlement, notifications, NUMI, Sentinel, reports and register kind are text that configures
#     nothing. Nineteen starting points are supplied, each with a form (six kinds of answer). A step raises no notice.
#   * Nothing runs on a schedule, nothing leaves the application, no outside system is connected.
#   * The sandbox (src/lib/sandbox.ts, src/pages/Sandbox.tsx) is the in-browser engine filled with a copy of the
#     configuration and of the balances; it copies no transaction, role or permission.
#   * Cross-cutting rules of the build (1482, 1484, 1497, 1518, 1526, 1551, 1554, 1555, 1916) are left as they were:
#     assessing them would mean assessing every module of every phase, which this reading did not do.
