    ("PARTIAL", 1517, "tests/sql/engine_invariants.sql T06 T10d T11e T11f T11g T16e · tests/numiOps.test.ts 'reports a refusal as a refusal and does not say whether records exist' · tests/sql/phase3_inventory.sql T168 T187 T189 · tests/sql/phase3_investments.sql T201 T205 T211 · tests/sql/phase3_control.sql T223 T235 T238 · tests/sql/phase3_platform.sql T244 T249 T254 T257 T258 T261 T262 T263 T266 T267 · tests/p3control.test.ts 'the example of the specification: 100 ordered, 100 billed, 82 received, 100 paid — reality does not reconcile' 'notices: what falls due is found when a person opens the application, and finding it again adds nothing' · tests/p3app.test.ts 'stock is refused to a person without the permission, whatever the records hold' 'a list of the live books is read to its end'",
     "Built: automated tests cover accounting (balance, posting and reversal, since Phase 1), permissions, tenant isolation (a company cannot write into, use the accounts of or open the journals of another, T11e to T11g), approvals, audit (the trail is append-only, T10d), idempotency (a posting repeated returns the same voucher, T06; an invoice approved twice posts once, T16e) and AI boundaries (NUMI reports a refusal as a refusal). Phase 3 adds: integrations — the register holds no secret and guards what can move money (T257); migration — an import is checked before it enters the books, enters as drafts and the earlier trial balance is compared ledger by ledger (T261 to T263); security — every table has row level security and the internal functions cannot be called by a signed-in user (T266, T267); reconciliation — the comparisons of NUMERO Reality (tested); multi-company — a simulation refuses the figures of a company the person may not read (T244); idempotency — finding what falls due again adds no notice (T254), the same days of a management fee cannot be charged twice (T205), the same difference is one case (T223), the same file is not committed twice (T262); every entry posted by the Phase 3 suites balances (T189, T211, T238). Not built: concurrency — no test runs two sessions at the same time (stock awaiting approval on one document is refused on another, T168, one after the other); the live data layer between the screens and the database has no automated test apart from its two list readers; no test drives a screen; integrations are tested as a register only, since none is connected."),

    ("PARTIAL", 1541, "src/pages/Imports.tsx · src/engine/analysis.ts parallelRun · src/api/demoPlatform.ts · supabase/migrations/0018_platform.sql stage_import, commit_import, discard_import, backup_checks, record_backup_check · src/pages/SystemHealth.tsx · tests/sql/phase3_platform.sql T260 T261 T262 T263 · tests/p3control.test.ts 'an import is checked before it enters the books, and enters them as drafts' 'the books of the earlier system beside NUMERO: ledger by ledger, and ready only when nothing differs'",
     "Built: nothing of this requirement was recorded as built before Phase 3. Phase 3 adds, for data brought in from an earlier system under Imports: validate — the file is staged and checked (every row, duplicates, debits against credits, mapping of accounts) and a file that fails a check cannot be committed (T261); migrate — journals and opening balances enter the books as drafts that are approved like any other entry, and the same file is not committed twice (T262); verify — the trial balance of the earlier system is kept beside the books and compared ledger by ledger (T263); a staged file can be discarded with a reason. Backups made by the database provider can be recorded under System Health (T260). Not built: NUMERO makes no backup before an import (it keeps what a person records); a committed file cannot be rolled back as a whole — the database refuses to discard it and says that what was committed is corrected in the books; the migrations of the database schema carry no rollback and move forward only."),

